This product includes software developed for biomedical terminology alignment.

BioSemAlign release artifacts do not bundle or redistribute terminology
content. The source repository may contain response cassettes used only for
hermetic tests; distribution-content checks exclude those cassettes from both
the wheel and source distribution. Users are responsible for reviewing the
terms that apply to any resource content they cache or redistribute:

  * RxNorm is developed by the U.S. National Library of Medicine. NLM's
    normalized names, identifiers, and relationships are public-domain
    material, while some source-vocabulary content available through broader
    UMLS/RxNorm distributions may remain proprietary.
  * UMLS requires an authorized UMLS Metathesaurus Licence and API key.
  * MedDRA, SNOMED CT, and other proprietary vocabularies require licences
    obtained directly from their respective owners.

See src/biosemalign/resources/registry.yaml for the packaged resource and
licence registry, and verify current upstream terms before publication.
